<style>
    body {
        font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
        background: #f7f7f7;
        color: #222;
    }

    .presentation {
        max-width: 1280px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 2rem 1.5rem 3rem;
    }

    .title {
        text-align: center;
        color: #0b4aa2;
        margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
        font-size: 2.2rem;
    }

    .slide {
        background: #fff;
        border: 1px solid #e5e5e5;
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
        margin: 1rem 0;
    }

    .slide h2 {
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        color: #0b4aa2;
        font-size: 1.4rem;
    }

    .slide p {
        margin: 0.4rem 0;
    }

    .code-block {
        background: #111;
        color: #eaeaea;
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
        font-family: "Courier New", monospace;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .tag {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
        border-radius: 999px;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-right: 0.35rem;
    }

    .get {
        background: #e7f7ee;
        color: #0b7a39;
    }

    .post {
        background: #e6f0ff;
        color: #1b56b3;
    }

    .delete {
        background: #ffe7e7;
        color: #b42323;
    }

    .two-col {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
        gap: 0.8rem;
    }

    .callout {
        background: #f2f7ff;
        border-left: 4px solid #0b4aa2;
        padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
        border-radius: 6px;
        margin: 0.6rem 0;
    }

    .small {
        color: #555;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
        .title {
            font-size: 1.9rem;
        }

        .slide {
            padding: 1rem;
        }
    }
</style>

<div class="presentation">
    <h1 class="title">Pseudocoder Rails Overview</h1>

    <section class="slide">
        <h2>1) What Rails + ERB means</h2>
        <p>ERB lets us embed Ruby in HTML to render dynamic content.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>&lt;% if current_user.present? %&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Welcome, &lt;%= current_user.name %&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;
</code></pre>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>&lt;% if @pseudocode_output.present? %&gt;
    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;%= @pseudocode_output %&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;% else %&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Please avoid submitting gibberish code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;
</code></pre>
        <p class="small">This pattern appears on our home page to show results only when they exist.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
        <h2>2) MVC and request flow</h2>
        <div class="callout">Browser -> Routes -> Controller -> Model -> View -> HTML</div>
        <p>Example: login hits <strong>SessionsController#create</strong>, checks the User model, then redirects.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code># sessions_controller.rb
def create
    user = User.find_by(email: params[:email])
    if user&.authenticate(params[:password])
        session[:user_id] = user.id
        redirect_to home_path
    else
        flash[:alert] = "Invalid email or password"
        redirect_to login_path
    end
end
</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
        <h2>3) Routes and HTTP verbs</h2>
        <div class="two-col">
            <div>
                <p><span class="tag get">GET</span>/login -> sessions#new</p>
                <p><span class="tag post">POST</span>/login -> sessions#create</p>
                <p><span class="tag delete">DELETE</span>/logout -> sessions#destroy</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <p><span class="tag post">POST</span>/compilations -> compilations#create</p>
                <p><span class="tag delete">DELETE</span>/compilations/:id -> compilations#destroy</p>
                <p><span class="tag post">POST</span>/contact_submit -> pages#contact_submit</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <pre class="code-block"><code># config/routes.rb
get "/login", to: "sessions#new"
post "/login", to: "sessions#create"
delete "/logout", to: "sessions#destroy"
resources :compilations, only: [:create, :destroy]
post "contact_submit", to: "pages#contact_submit"
</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
        <h2>4) Users, bcrypt, and password_digest</h2>
        <p>We store hashed passwords in <strong>password_digest</strong> using bcrypt.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>class User &lt; ApplicationRecord
  has_secure_password
  validates :email, presence: true, uniqueness: true
  validates :password, length: { minimum: 6 }, if: -> { password.present? }
end
</code></pre>
        <pre class="code-block"><code># login check
user = User.find_by(email: params[:email])
user.authenticate(params[:password])
</code></pre>
        <p class="small">has_secure_password adds <strong>authenticate(password)</strong> for login checks.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
        <h2>5) Compilations: core feature flow</h2>
        <p>Users submit code or upload a file. The compiler service generates pseudocode and we save it for logged-in users.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>if params[:file].present?
  output_text = Compiler.compile(uploaded_file, from_file: true)
elsif params[:code].present?
  output_text = Compiler.compile(input_text, from_file: false)
end

current_user.compilations.create!(
  input_type: input_type,
  input_text: input_text,
  output_text: output_text
)
</code></pre>
        <pre class="code-block"><code># compilation.rb
class Compilation &lt; ApplicationRecord
    belongs_to :user
    validates :input_text, presence: true
    validates :output_text, presence: true
end
</code></pre>
        <p class="small">Errors like unsupported language or syntax errors are handled with clear messages.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
        <h2>6) Password reset and email change</h2>
        <p>We use secure tokens for password reset and email change confirmation.</p>
        <div class="two-col">
            <div>
                <p><strong>Password reset</strong></p>
                <pre class="code-block"><code>def generate_reset_token
  self.reset_token = SecureRandom.hex(32)
  self.reset_token_expires_at = 1.hour.from_now
  save
end
</code></pre>
                <pre class="code-block"><code># password_resets_controller.rb
def create
    user = User.find_by(email: params[:email])
    if user
        user.generate_reset_token
        UserMailer.password_reset_email(user).deliver_now
    end
end
</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div>
                <p><strong>Email change</strong></p>
                <pre class="code-block"><code>def initiate_email_change(new_email)
  self.pending_email = new_email
  self.email_confirmation_token = SecureRandom.hex(32)
  save
end
</code></pre>
                <pre class="code-block"><code># email_changes_controller.rb
def create
    user = current_user
    if user.initiate_email_change(params[:new_email])
        UserMailer.email_change_confirmation(user).deliver_now
    end
end
</code></pre>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="small">Mailers send links to finish the flow.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="slide">
        <h2>7) Contact form + database quick look</h2>
        <p>Contact page posts to <strong>/contact_submit</strong> and sends email via <strong>ContactMailer</strong>.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>&lt;form action="/contact_submit" method="POST"&gt;
  &lt;%= hidden_field_tag :authenticity_token, form_authenticity_token %&gt;
  &lt;input type="text" name="firstname" required&gt;
  &lt;input type="email" name="email" required&gt;
  &lt;textarea name="subject" required&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>
        <pre class="code-block"><code># contact_mailer.rb
mail(
  from: email,
  to: "theofficialpseudocoder@gmail.com",
  subject: "Customer Support Request"
)
</code></pre>
        <div class="two-col">
            <div>
                <p><strong>Users table</strong></p>
                <p class="small">email, name, password_digest, reset_token</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <p><strong>Compilations table</strong></p>
                <p class="small">user_id, input_type, input_text, output_text</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>